abstract: >-
  A full-stack demonstration web application for peptide-MHC class I binding
  prediction, providing an interactive research interface for single-sequence
  prediction, batch processing, mutation impact analysis, and peptide design,
  built with React and Express.js. Predictions currently shown by the running
  application are illustrative placeholders and are not produced by a trained
  model. A separate model (XGBoost baseline and ESM-2 150M + LoRA, held-out
  ROC-AUC 0.919 / 0.922 respectively, trained offline on MHCflurry curated
  data with a leak-free peptide-grouped split) is being integrated into this
  application; those figures describe offline evaluation of that model, not
  the current output of this software.
